      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## W7 image SR v1 (TEST) - Kandinsky ImageSR 2.0 x2, native nodes\n\n- Put the image in `input/motion/sr/`, pick it in **Image to upscale**, run. Output: `output/motion/sr/<name>_kandinsky-x2_*.png` + `<name>_bicubic-x2_*.png` (baseline, for the side by side).\n- The model file is a native conversion (`convert_kandinsky_sr.py`) for **t = 0.15** (x2 default, creativity 4). **t must match** in 3 places: the model file, **Latent gain** (1/(1-t)) and **ManualSigmas** (`t, 0`). Keep bicubic x2, euler, no noise.\n- The prompt is ignored (the text path is zeroed); the encoders are loaded only because the native Kandinsky 5 needs them.\n- No 1024 px tiling (the official pipeline tiles): the whole image goes in one pass. 1088x1920 -> 2176x3840.\n- License: MIT (model and code)."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## W7 image SR v1 (TEST) - Kandinsky ImageSR 2.0 x2, native nodes\n\n- Put the image in `input/motion/sr/`, pick it in **Image to upscale**, run. Output: `output/motion/sr/<name>_kandinsky-x2_*.png` + `<name>_bicubic-x2_*.png` (baseline, for the side by side).\n- The model file is a native conversion (`convert_kandinsky_sr.py`) for **t = 0.15** (x2 default, creativity 4). **t must match** in 3 places: the model file, **Latent gain** (1/(1-t)) and **ManualSigmas** (`t, 0`). Keep bicubic x2, euler, no noise.\n- The prompt is ignored (the text path is zeroed); the encoders are loaded only because the native Kandinsky 5 needs them.\n- No 1024 px tiling (the official pipeline tiles): the whole image goes in one pass. 1088x1920 -> 2176x3840.\n- License: MIT (model and code)."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
